1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:03,640
So the Special Crimes
Division is having a big day

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,680
I knew you'd still be worried about Ryo-chan

3
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:13,360
Don't be ridiculous,
who's worried about that guy?

4
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:15,819
But Chief,

5
00:00:15,869 --> 00:00:20,560
at this rate, Senpai will end up staying in
the Special Crimes Division for good, won't he?

6
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:23,720
Yeah, he seems to be fitting in pretty well,
doesn't he?

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:25,540
You think so?

8
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:25,960
Yes.

9
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,920
I just remembered something I had to do.

10
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:31,320
I'm heading out.

11
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:38,520
Oof, there we go.

12
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:39,520
Damn it.

13
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,020
They're using people as disposable pawns,
the bastards.

14
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:44,580
I'm not putting up with being an apprentice.

15
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:51,540
Ouch!

16
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:52,320
Ow

17
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:54,720
Good to see you,

18
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:56,960
Chief.

19
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:58,580
Ryotsu.

20
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:01,740
What are you doing in a place like this?

21
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:06,260
Don't tell me you've come to apologize
after reflecting on your actions.

22
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:10,120
Well, if you apologize,
I suppose I might not refuse to go back.

23
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:11,860
Don't be ridiculous.

24
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:14,500
What are you doing in a
place like this yourself?

25
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,080
No, I'm not...

26
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:20,060
If you want to come back to the police box,
I suppose I could listen to your request.

27
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:21,180
Who'd ever do that?

28
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:24,980
Unlike the chief of some police box,
the Special Crimes Division chief

29
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:26,800
is so kind, isn't he?

30
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:27,900
What did you say?

31
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:30,960
Now that the troublemaker is gone from here,

32
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:32,660
I'm finally relieved.

33
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:34,420
I see.

34
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:35,940
Well, that's good to hear.

35
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:57,863
Since I can't return to my post,

36
00:01:57,913 --> 00:02:00,620
we've got to make this place
more comfortable somehow.

37
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:08,591
Hey,

38
00:02:08,641 --> 00:02:12,580
Section Chief, we've arrived.

39
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,540
Why are you panicking?

40
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:20,800
Ow ow ow! What the hell are you doing?

41
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:25,000
Aaaaaah!

42
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,700
Aaaaaah, sorry!
I won't do anything to the Section Chief!

43
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:41,060
What's that heart flapping its wings?

44
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:42,860
It's the Section Chief's wife.

45
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:44,920
What, you got married?

46
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:12,600
Why were those two fighting?

47
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:16,620
Apparently there were another hen's
lips on the Section Chief's body.

48
00:03:16,620 --> 00:03:18,940
The one from the car earlier.

49
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:22,380
Even so, the Section Chief is
completely under his wife's thumb.

50
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:26,340
Good to know.

51
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:33,680
The powers that be are full of corruption,
and they run wild with it.

52
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:36,600
In a world where you
don't know what to believe,

53
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:41,260
I always believed the Chief
and Ryo-san were the best team.

54
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:43,560
Me and that idiot?

55
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:46,360
Sure, they're always fighting.

56
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:49,822
Yeah, being able to clash
that openly with each other,

57
00:03:49,872 --> 00:03:51,980
you don't even see that between
parent and child these days.

58
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,200
I'm sure Ryo-san is itching to come back.

59
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:58,520
Y-you think so?

60
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:01,780
Of course. He's just being stubborn.

61
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:05,300
Why don't you treat him to one, Chief?

62
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:11,460
Yeah.

63
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:35,040
Hey, Section Chief.

64
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:38,500
Promote me from apprentice to police constable
in the Criminal Investigation Division.

65
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:42,620
He says that's not possible.

66
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:44,946
If you don't like it, that's fine.

67
00:04:44,996 --> 00:04:48,000
I'll just show this photo to your wife.

68
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:54,100
Anything but that.
He says it's a lifelong favor.

69
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:57,520
So you'll recognize me as a detective
in the Special Crimes Division, then.

70
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,400
Yes, understood.

71
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:05,180
Good. From now on,
you'll be considered my subordinate, got it?

72
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:08,020
That's a bit...

73
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:11,000
Then, off to your wife's place now.

74
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:15,940
Fine, I'll do as you say,
so please forgive me.

75
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:20,720
Alright, from now on I'll control the
Special Crimes Division from behind the scenes!

76
00:05:21,580 --> 00:05:27,040
This is Katsushika Police Station.

77
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:30,340
We'll lure them here and
take them all down at once.

78
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:35,000
Taking over a police station,
that's quite bold, boss.

79
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,500
Revenge is better when it's flashy.

80
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:39,840
Now, go!

81
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,740
Sunlight from the sky?

82
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:45,820
Undoshi from the land,

83
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:49,260
and Shark from the sea.

84
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:50,340
The sea?

85
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:52,300
We don't have a sea.

86
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:54,300
Mommy!

87
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:02,640
Even without a sea,
as long as there's water, we can invade!

88
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:11,760
Well, it's been like
a wake every single day.

89
00:06:12,620 --> 00:06:23,100
Didn't you say you'd fired him and transferred him?
Ahhhh, I don't mind, but the officers at the police box have lost all their energy.

90
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:31,920
Saying all that, now that there's no one to scold, you're the one who's bored the most, right?
Yes, that's exactly right.

91
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:38,020
Hahaha, alright. Contact the Special Crimes
Division and have him return to his post.

92
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:54,640
Why would someone break
into a police station?

93
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:59,920
This is serious!

94
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:03,020
Suddenly, a huge amount of water and some kind
of gimmick came up through the first-floor floor.

95
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:04,100
What?!

96
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,540
Ohara.

97
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:09,820
Hands up!

98
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:15,740
You there, if you don't stay quiet,
you'll end up with a hole in you.

99
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:16,640
Yo!

100
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:26,700
We've just taken over the Katsushika police box.
Who the hell are you, and what's your purpose at the Katsushika police box?

101
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:30,220
Me? Just passing by.

102
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:33,880
You're...

103
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:40,220
Living the easy life!

104
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:45,080
Yeah, yeah,
this is the Special Crimes Division...

105
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:50,020
What? The police box has been taken over?

106
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:54,640
This is the crime claim video we
just received from the culprits.

107
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,560
Now, the revenge film presents!

108
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:02,440
Starring FundoC

109
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:03,660
T-this man...

110
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:06,740
That's the violent
criminal I arrested before!

111
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:08,460
Shark

112
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:12,180
This is the sea-hijacker I busted.

113
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:13,700
Annico

114
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:15,640
T-this woman is...

115
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:18,100
arrested by our magnificent transformation!

116
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,020
Inchiki Rebaishi

117
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:21,720
Kaipan Deka

118
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,760
Dolphin Deka

119
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:23,780
Ekkō Deka

120
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:25,200
Long time no see

121
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:29,500
We're also the ones who took down
those topknot-wearing section chiefs.

122
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:30,360
What?

123
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,360
Look at that!

124
00:08:34,060 --> 00:08:35,500
The Chief and the Station Chief.

125
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:37,860
If you want the hostages to live,

126
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:39,640
their lives will cost you 300 million yen.

127
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:41,480
You three, come alone.

128
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:43,120
And bring the way to take them off, too.

129
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:45,060
We'll give you a good working over.

130
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:49,180
That's all.

131
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:51,160
Well, this is bad.

132
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:52,900
The Chief is being held hostage, and

133
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:55,080
Someone like you is fired!

134
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:56,960
I'm quitting today!

135
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:00,760
Right, Shirimoto, is it?

136
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,740
Let's all section chiefs storm in together.

137
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:08,980
No, the culprits said
only you lot should come,

138
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:10,760
so you lot should go alone.

139
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:11,300
What?

140
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:15,480
The Section Chief and I have other work,
don't we?

141
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:22,660
Understood. Just us will be enough.

142
00:09:22,660 --> 00:09:23,660
Let's go.

143
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:24,660
Yeah.

144
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:40,900
Damn! The station's inside
is flooded with water!

145
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:43,120
Is a frontal breakthrough impossible?

146
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:43,740
Through the back, then?

147
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:47,660
I've prepared the 300 million yen ransom,
just in case.

148
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:49,940
Thank you.

149
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:52,700
As expected of the Nakagawa Group's heir.

150
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:54,700
Why hasn't Ryo-chan come?

151
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:56,940
Apparently he has other work to do.

152
00:09:57,500 --> 00:10:00,700
That's outrageous!
The Chief's life is in danger!

153
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:03,040
I'll go get Ryo-chan!

154
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,240
I'm coming with you!

155
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:05,780
Alright, let's all go together!

156
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:12,000
Have they arrived? By Gekkō?

157
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,640
Open a breach for us!

158
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:19,020
Let's go, Venus! Operation start!

159
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:19,940
Roger!

160
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:29,400
I am the champion! Missile Fatch!

161
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:30,580
What?

162
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:36,240
Moonlight Detective! Venus Detective!

163
00:10:41,460 --> 00:10:43,260
Moonlight Detective! Venus Detective!

164
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:45,520
I'm all right! I'm safe, somehow!

165
00:10:50,660 --> 00:10:51,960
Leave this to me.

166
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:54,620
We'll infiltrate through
the underground waterway.

167
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:07,020
Infiltration successful.

168
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:08,480
Here comes Dolphin!

169
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:17,060
How dare you do this!

170
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:18,560
Eat this torpedo!

171
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:20,620
Don't let them!

172
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:24,720
The torpedo!

173
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:28,980
I can see through all your attacks!

174
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:34,260
You're just going to stand there and watch my
cute little dolphin minions become shark food!

175
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:47,140
Stop it!

176
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,600
Go out and gather more, and more!

177
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,940
Say I have a million henchmen,

178
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:03,240
each one bringing in just 10 yen,

179
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:06,520
and in no time, 10 million yen will be mine.

180
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,900
Ryo-chan, what are you doing?

181
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:12,260
What is this? Who are you people?

182
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:15,000
Senpai, why won't you come?

183
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,120
The Chief is being held hostage, you know!

184
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:19,020
He's not even our superior anymore.

185
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:24,920
That's none of our business! What are you saying?
Chief, so that Ryo-chan can return to his post...

186
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:29,180
He went to bow his head to the station chief and got caught up in this incident,
you know. What?

187
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:34,900
Ryo-san, go help the Chief!
Ryo-san, please come with us!

188
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:40,520
Well, we're just relieved
the troublemaker's gone.

189
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:43,840
Like I care!

190
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,080
I'm busy.

191
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:45,800
Just go home.

192
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:46,440
Ryo-chan.

193
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:48,840
I never thought Ryo-sama
was that kind of person.

194
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:50,900
I misjudged you, senior.

195
00:12:50,900 --> 00:12:52,280
Let's all go home.

196
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:54,540
Let's rescue the Chief with our own hands.

197
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:56,580
Ryo-chan, you idiot.

198
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:04,540
Are you sure about that?

199
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:13,780
Hahahaha

200
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:15,460
Hahaha

201
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:17,340
*Rolls eyes back*

202
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,520
Hahahaha

203
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:20,720
Chief

204
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:24,040
Forget collecting petty cash!

205
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:26,700
Tengen, urgently gather the team!

206
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:31,740
He says the preparations
are already complete.

207
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:32,400
What?

208
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,120
What is it?

209
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:39,420
Wow, amazing! Tengen!

210
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:43,940
Alright, let's go, Degemon!

211
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:49,220
The return of the Patrol Poppo Detective!

212
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:58,360
It's only a matter of time before that
Dolphin bastard becomes shark bait.

213
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:02,260
All that's left is to take down Kaipan
Deka and collect the 300 million yen.

214
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,040
Come out, you criminal scum!

215
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:11,480
Hahahaha!

216
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,300
Think you're scared yet, you villains!

217
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:14,842
Ryotsu, Kankichi,

218
00:14:14,892 --> 00:14:17,780
No, wait, I mean...
Hato-poppo! I mean, Kenzo's here!

219
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,040
R-Ryotsu!

220
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:21,380
Never mind! Take him out too!

221
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:21,900
Yeah!

222
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:24,940
Back off!

223
00:14:43,353 --> 00:14:47,260
Pinka-chan

224
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:49,700
It's a message from
Detective Hatopoppo, nanoda.

225
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:53,020
If you buy the shark too,
there's nothing to be scared of, nanoda.

226
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:54,400
What?

227
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:55,760
I see.

228
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:57,480
Right, understood.

229
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,300
That one...

230
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:05,000
Huh?

231
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:08,760
Vinyl...

232
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:11,700
Stop!

233
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,480
Use this, nanoda!

234
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:29,560
Thanks, Pinka-chan! Alright!

235
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:12,360
So the pervert shows his face.

236
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:14,740
This one is my opponent.

237
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:18,320
Kaipan Deka!

238
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:20,740
I've been waiting so long for this day.

239
00:16:20,740 --> 00:16:23,040
Today I'll finally settle the score.

240
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:26,440
It's a naked duel, man to man.

241
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,320
Very well.

242
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,660
Hey, Kaipan!

243
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:38,980
I'm challenging you man to man,
naked to naked, one on one.

244
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:45,820
Whoa, what?

245
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:49,060
It's time to refuel with energy.

246
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:51,160
I told you, stop with the bananas!

247
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:53,060
What a brilliant attack.

248
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:55,140
But if you're going with bananas,

249
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:59,400
then I'm bringing the muskmelon.

250
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:03,820
W-what are you thinking?

251
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:07,860
You got me there.

252
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:11,440
Don't go down that easily, dammit.

253
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:17,420
Whoa!

254
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:21,680
Nin!

255
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:24,220
Looks like a... (ara, esasou)

256
00:17:26,150 --> 00:17:28,220
So what, then?

257
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:32,700
What a brilliant attack.

258
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:36,180
But that won't take me down.

259
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:36,680
What?

260
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,020
Gyaaah!

261
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:45,280
Take my attack!

262
00:17:51,560 --> 00:17:54,020
What's the point of all this, anyway?

263
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:57,020
How about that?

264
00:17:58,500 --> 00:18:00,020
I lose!

265
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:03,780
How about it? You can't keep up with me!
Let's go, it's pretty huge, isn't it?

266
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:09,560
Chief

267
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:10,980
Alright!

268
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:12,960
The Chief and the culprit are

269
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:16,420
The culprit fled to the
rooftop with Ohare-kun.

270
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:18,380
The rooftop

271
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:25,320
You're still alive Pretty big,
aren't you, Venus?

272
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,620
This woman is kind of dangerous!

273
00:18:27,620 --> 00:18:30,940
Hey, you dared to shoot down Moonlight,
didn't you?

274
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:33,160
This time I'll finish you off for good!

275
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:36,980
Moonlight Power!

276
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:40,560
Reiker!

277
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:45,320
Here we go again, aren't we?

278
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:49,680
Tekumaku Mayakin,
Tekumaku Mayakin, become a yokozuna!

279
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:56,580
You're just changing clothes too,
aren't you?

280
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:00,920
Henshin! Gekkō Deka!

281
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:05,405
Allow me to explain! By transforming into a women's pro wrestling girl,
Gekkō Deka

282
00:19:05,455 --> 00:19:07,840
can unleash incredible power and skill!

283
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:09,500
Woohoo!

284
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:15,772
I'll explain it myself!
I transform into Yokozuna Akemono,

285
00:19:15,822 --> 00:19:18,660
and with Rocket Halte,
I'll settle my years-old grudge!

286
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:19,460
Go for it!

287
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:21,580
Whoa! Rocket Halte!

288
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:29,020
Gekkō Deka!

289
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:34,360
Gekkō Deka!

290
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,960
All talk and no action.

291
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:40,460
Damn it!
Then I'll take on Hatopoppo Deka myself!

292
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:42,880
Genemon,
use the pea-shooter plan on the pigeons!

293
00:19:43,940 --> 00:19:44,260
What?

294
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:50,920
What?

295
00:19:57,620 --> 00:20:00,720
So it's not "scissors bean-shooter,
" it's "dove bean-shooter," isn't it!

296
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:03,800
That's the takedown from before!

297
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:07,220
Yes!

298
00:20:07,900 --> 00:20:09,480
It's too early to celebrate!

299
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:11,740
C-Chief!

300
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:13,240
Ryotsu!

301
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:17,120
Kankichi Ryotsu, I'm going to
settle the score from last time!

302
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:19,960
Score from last time? Who are you?

303
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:23,560
Wh-who are you?

304
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:25,480
Who was it again?

305
00:20:27,620 --> 00:20:30,240
I'm Abutarakatabura from the summer special!

306
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:34,240
There you are!
You're so forgettable, I forgot about you.

307
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:37,660
Because of you and the Special Investigations Division,
I went through hell.

308
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:39,180
My little brother still wasn't giving up.

309
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:42,220
This whole incident was set up by this guy.

310
00:20:42,740 --> 00:20:44,020
So that's how it was.

311
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:47,080
You lose, Ryotsu!

312
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,160
We'll see about that.

313
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:54,760
Don't you dare come closer,
or this guy's life is over!

314
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:57,500
Whoa, it's Ryotsu!

315
00:20:57,500 --> 00:21:00,080
Can you hear me? I'm really going to shoot!

316
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:01,780
Be my guest.

317
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:02,880
W-what?

318
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:06,240
A boss who dotes on his
cactus more than me...

319
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:08,380
I couldn't care less what happens to him.

320
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:09,640
Ryotsu...

321
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:11,700
Come on, go ahead and shoot!

322
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:13,560
I don't mind at all.

323
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:16,700
Why don't you ask a
cactus to help you instead?

324
00:21:16,700 --> 00:21:18,100
Hey, Bochu.

325
00:21:18,100 --> 00:21:20,440
Ryotsu!

326
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:22,020
Hey!

327
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:23,180
Sorry!

328
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:26,440
I won't forgive you, you bastard!

329
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:28,240
You, you bastard...

330
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:29,440
Chief! Hang in there!

331
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,880
Shut up! How dare you talk about me like -

332
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:33,480
It was a plan! A plan!

333
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:34,840
A plan?

334
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:36,820
We deliberately made the Chief angry

335
00:21:36,820 --> 00:21:39,680
so he'd knock that guy out.
That was the plan.

336
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,940
I thought I was going to die.

337
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,740
When did you get here?

338
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:48,340
Come on! Wasn't it you, Chief, who did it?

339
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:49,820
Me?

340
00:21:49,820 --> 00:21:52,760
I know your personality
inside and out, Chief.

341
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:54,980
I was sure you'd do it.

342
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,340
Ryotsu!

343
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:00,360
What's wrong, Chief?

344
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:06,200
Say what you like,
but you came to save me after all.

345
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:06,800
Thank you.

346
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:11,160
Chief, I'm the one who should apologize.
I'm sorry about your precious cactus.

347
00:22:11,160 --> 00:22:12,380
It's fine.

348
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:14,800
Then you'll come back
to the police box, right?

349
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,280
Yes.

350
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:18,040
I see.

351
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:20,760
Congratulations!

352
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:23,440
Everyone!

353
00:22:30,560 --> 00:22:33,580
By the way, Degemon, about this photo...

354
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:38,120
He's saying, "Please stop, have mercy!"

355
00:22:39,460 --> 00:22:42,260
Don't get the wrong idea,
this is what I'll do!

356
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:43,120
There you go.

357
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:46,900
Hey, Ryotsu.

358
00:22:46,900 --> 00:22:49,240
What was that just now?

359
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:52,160
It's nothing.

360
00:22:52,620 --> 00:22:55,220
Instead, why don't we go
out and have a big time today?

361
00:22:55,700 --> 00:22:57,300
That sounds good.

362
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:59,720
And today we're saying goodbye to Ryotsu.

363
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:03,560
Alright, I'll treat you,
so let's have a hotpot party.

364
00:23:03,560 --> 00:23:06,840
Sounds good. Then how about a yami-nabe?

365
00:23:08,120 --> 00:23:09,940
Dummy boy!

366
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:12,320
I was just joking!

367
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:13,560
Butcher!

368
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:31,200
Startled and making a fuss,

369
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:34,160
solved by talking it through.

370
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:37,200
Quick, and pour in the broth.

371
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:42,960
Decided, and a flash of inspiration.

372
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:47,340
Bouncing along, wrapping it up,
and taking action.

373
00:23:47,340 --> 00:23:53,480
Flying off, the most amazing power of all.

374
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:59,580
Everyone gather, if you come here.

375
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:06,060
A dreamlike, final energy.

376
00:24:07,300 --> 00:24:10,260
Chase down tomorrow, believe in yesterday.

377
00:24:10,260 --> 00:24:16,540
Drawing the universe and standing on the earth,
the star of Kameari spun around in a circle.

378
00:24:16,540 --> 00:24:19,920
Speedy!

379
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:25,220
Brave, and flapping wings,
and checking, and taking a stance...

380
00:24:25,220 --> 00:24:28,520
Akiri and heart and Ribuli.

381
00:24:28,520 --> 00:24:29,780
Getting fired up!

382
00:24:31,280 --> 00:24:38,980
Bah-fun, here it comes, a rush welling up,
pulling it off, turning around, and spinning.

383
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:10,240
BGM

384
00:25:10,740 --> 00:25:13,580
"This is good, right?" "Like hell it is!"

